{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>The first of the first fruits of your land.</b> From the seven species mentioned in praise of your land — ״a land of wheat and barley and vine, etc.״ (Deuteronomy 8) — and the honey is date honey." "<b>You shall not cook a kid.</b> A warning against meat in milk. And it is written three times in the Torah: one for eating, one for deriving benefit, and one for the prohibition of cooking (Ḥullin 115)." "<b>Kid.</b> Any young offspring is in its meaning — even a calf and a lamb. From the fact that Scripture needed to specify in several places ״גְּדִי עִזִּים,״ you learn that גְּדִי unstated means every nursing young in its meaning (ibid. 113)." "<b>In its mother's milk.</b> Excludes fowl, which has no milk — its prohibition is not from the Torah but from rabbinic enactment (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:38.065446648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}